# Pipeline working directory: the 317 MB Met CSV, the National Gallery CSVs and
# the resumable append logs. Regenerable from scratch with
# pipeline/00_download_csv.sh + stages 01-05.
/data/

# Committed on purpose (GitHub Pages serves them directly, and re-deriving them
# would mean re-downloading 7,094 images from four museums on every clone):
#   app/data/chromatica.json     1.2 MB, 351 KB over the wire
#   app/thumbs/{src}/{id}.webp   7,094 files, 249 MB
#   app/og.png                   the social preview card, built by stage 06
#
# That 249 MB is the standing cost of this repository, and it is paid once per
# rendering of the set, forever: git keeps every version of every binary, so a
# rerun of stage 05 at a different size or quality does not replace the old
# thumbnails, it adds a second copy of all 7,094 to the history. The rule that
# follows is: re-render only for a change of format or dimensions that is worth
# a permanent doubling, never to retouch quality. THUMB_QUALITY was settled by
# measurement (see config.py) precisely so that it would not have to move.

.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store
